      "title": "سلاحف شاطئ شرمة",
      "est_minutes": 20,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "markdown_ar": "اقرأ عن **السلاحف البحرية** في شاطئ **شرمة** شرق المكلا، ثم أجب عن الأسئلة. ستجد أفعالاً جديدة؛ ركّز على المعلومات المطلوبة."
        },
        {
          "type": "video",
          "youtube_id": "Th9S81mblxo",
          "video_title": "مفردات عن الحيوانات — الحلقة 6",
          "channel": "ZAmericanEnglish",
          "channel_url": "https://www.youtube.com/@ZAmericanEnglish",
          "duration_sec": 502,
          "optional": true,
          "approx_size_mb": 33
        },
        {
          "type": "reading",
          "text_en": "Every year, between January and June, something special happens at Sharma beach, east of Mukalla. Big green sea turtles come out of the sea at night. Each turtle digs a hole in the sand and lays about one hundred eggs. Then she goes back to the sea. After two months, the baby turtles come out of the eggs and walk to the water. The baby turtles are very small and many animals eat them, like birds and crabs. Local people and volunteers protect the beach. They don't use lights near the turtles, and they don't touch the eggs. Sharma is one of the most important places for turtles in the Arabian Sea.",
          "word_count": 112
        },
